.TH TRAP 1.SH NAMEtrap \- an example trap handler.SH SYNOPSIS\fB/dd/CMDS/trap\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONAn example of writing an OS-9 trap handler in C, with\fBtraptst\fRbeside it in\fBSRC/trap\fRto call it.  The module installs its trap from system state, so startedfrom the shell as an ordinary program it is entered and stops on thefirst supervisor-only instruction; that refusal is all it can showoutside a system build.  Name it by its pathlist:\fBtrap\fRis also a shell built-in..SH SEE ALSOt